ator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, across 8 grids. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, November to December came in under 90% of normal in 37 years, the most of any pair. In 2025 the middle ran 186% of normal in May to June and 44% in November to December. So far in 2026 it sat at 50% in February to March, and a preliminary estimate for grid 17563 puts August to September 2026 at 42.2.</p>"}
